1
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:07,030
This video shows you how to find which step set or changed a field.

2
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:11,390
You're in firewall-parse, with records you captured from firewall.

3
00:00:11,440 --> 00:00:13,846
This record says risk is high.

4
00:00:13,846 --> 00:00:16,370
Which step decided that?

5
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:21,306
Each field has a sign beside it that names the step that last changed it.

6
00:00:21,306 --> 00:00:23,150
Hover it to see the step.

7
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:24,582
Click the sign.

8
00:00:24,582 --> 00:00:26,150
The step opens.

9
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:29,918
A denied connection to port 22 gets high.

10
00:00:29,918 --> 00:00:33,030
This one was denied, to port 22.

11
00:00:33,080 --> 00:00:36,568
A field can be changed by more than one step.

12
00:00:36,568 --> 00:00:40,470
user.name came from the parser, then the rename.

13
00:00:40,520 --> 00:00:43,089
To find the records one step changed,

14
00:00:43,089 --> 00:00:47,369
pause after it, and keep only rows changed by a step.

15
00:00:55,040 --> 00:00:59,483
Every record left here had its risk set by this step.

16
00:01:00,480 --> 00:01:02,428
Check on learning.

17
00:01:02,628 --> 00:01:05,597
The sign beside a field is the Code step's.

18
00:01:05,597 --> 00:01:07,854
What does that tell you?

19
00:01:12,254 --> 00:01:17,206
The Code step was the last step to set or change that field.

20
00:01:18,106 --> 00:01:22,714
Next, find the original of a record that already arrived.
